            }
          ],
          "text": "Going to somewhere"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "To go to somewhere, we use んかい or かい both are interchangeable in this context."
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For example:"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "しるし"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            },
            {
              "type": "underline"
            }
          ],
          "text": "(ん)かい"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "　いちゅん。 (To go to the mark)"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "かーら"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            },
            {
              "type": "underline"
            }
          ],
          "text": "(ん)かい"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "　ちゅーん。 (To come to the river / I am going/coming to the river)"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "しるし = mark, かーら = river, いちゅん = to go, ちゅーん = to come."
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Note here いちゅん is go, but the speaker is not going. So it either refers to either the listener or a third party going somewhere or when combined with other thing via conjugations (see the Intermediate 1 course) it can also mean a desire for the speaker to want to go somewhere (but is unable to)."
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "ちゅーん is come (for any party), but it can also mean that the speaker is physically going."
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
